WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
A five-metre ladder leans against a wall at about 37 degrees to the ground.
How high does it reach?

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
From the ground angle, the height is opposite, the ground distance is adjacent,
and the ladder is the hypotenuse.

00:12.000 --> 00:19.000
Sine is opposite over hypotenuse. Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse.
Tangent is opposite over adjacent.

00:19.000 --> 00:27.000
Use sine to find the height: five times sine of 37 degrees is about 3.01 metres.

00:27.000 --> 00:34.000
Cosine gives the ground distance: about 3.99 metres.
Tangent relates the height to the ground distance.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
Your turn: a ten-metre ladder makes the same angle. How high does it reach?
The length doubles, so the height doubles.
